          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Conduct a survey of vehicles in your neighbourhood."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.175,
            0.883,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Which types of vehicles are there? What types of fuels do they use?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.22,
            0.859,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Record the information that you collect in Table 11.3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.286,
            0.876,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.351,
                0.255,
                0.788,
                0.277
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Table 11.3: Types of vehicles and fuels used"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.262,
                0.286,
                0.876,
                0.454
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_table_8.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>Type of vehicle</td><td>Type of fuel used</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td rowspan=2></td></tr><tr><td></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.467,
            0.883,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the most common types of fuels used? Petrol and diesel are the two most widely used fuels for vehicles. Petrol, diesel and kerosene are obtained from petroleum. Petroleum along with natural gas and coal are commonly called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "fossil fuels.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " They are formed essentially from the remains of microorganisms and plants that got buried deep inside the earth, and were converted to petroleum, natural gas and coal. It takes millions of years for these fuels to form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.631,
            0.885,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Natural gas is used for cooking and generating electricity. Nowadays, it is also used in the form of Compressed Natural Gas (CNG) as a fuel for vehicles. It is a cleaner fuel than petrol or diesel. Coal is mainly used for the production of electricity. It is found in several parts of India. Find out the major coal-producing states and mark them in a map of India."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.866,
            0.286,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you know?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.324,
            0.819,
            0.789,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Earlier, coal, wood and dung cakes were used as fuels for cooking. Nowadays, less polluting natural gas and Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) have gradually replaced these domestic fuels."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
